  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain, the sum, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & =1\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(1)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot 0+2y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}{|}_{(2,\\sqrt{5})} & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}+\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+5}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{4+5}} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
